  <section class="section section--paper">
    <div class="container">
      <div class="insights-grid" id="insightList">
        <article class="icard icard--feature filterable reveal" id="renewable-energy-framework-2026" data-topic="energy" data-type="Article" data-author="Partner, Energy">
          <div class="icard-media">
            <img src="https://resource.scp-law.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/08/WhatsApp-Image-2026-08-14-at-10.04.02-AM.jpeg" alt="" loading="lazy" decoding="async" />
            <span class="icard-flag">Latest</span>
            <span class="icard-type">Article</span>
          </div>
          <div class="icard-body">
            <p class="icard-meta"><time>16 August 2026</time><span class="icard-sep" aria-hidden="true"></span><span class="icard-author">Partner, Energy</span></p>
            <h3 class="icard-title">No Shortcuts to Court: The NICN Reinforces Mandatory ADR in Employment/Trade Disputes</h3>
            <p class="icard-desc">Parties to employment and trade disputes are often eager to head straight to court. Nigerian law generally takes a different view.</p>
            <span class="icard-cta">Read<svg class="icard-arrow" viewBox="0 0 20 20" width="14" height="14" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false"><path d="M3 10h13M11 5l5 5-5 5" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.6" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"/></svg></span>
          </div>
          <a class="icard-link" href="#renewable-energy-framework-2026" data-track="article:open:renewable-energy-framework-2026" aria-label="Read: No Shortcuts to Court: The NICN Reinforces Mandatory ADR in Employment/Trade Disputes"><span class="sr-only">Read: No Shortcuts to Court: The NICN Reinforces Mandatory ADR in Employment/Trade Disputes</span></a>
        </article>
        <article class="icard filterable reveal" id="fccpc-merger-thresholds" data-topic="competition-law" data-type="Article" data-author="Partner, Competition">
          <div class="icard-media">
            <img src="https://resource.scp-law.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/08/WhatsApp-Image-2026-08-14-at-7.55.12-AM.jpeg" alt="" loading="lazy" decoding="async" />
            <span class="icard-type">Article</span>
          </div>
          <div class="icard-body">
            <p class="icard-meta"><time>16 August 2026</time><span class="icard-sep" aria-hidden="true"></span><span class="icard-author">Partner, Competition</span></p>
            <h3 class="icard-title">Your Letterhead Is Now a Compliance Document &mdash; Is It Ready?</h3>
            <p class="icard-desc">Under CAMA 2020, letters, invoices, receipts and notices must carry prescribed statutory information &mdash; an obligation enforcement has long left unchecked.</p>
            <span class="icard-cta">Read<svg class="icard-arrow" viewBox="0 0 20 20" width="14" height="14" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false"><path d="M3 10h13M11 5l5 5-5 5" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.6" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"/></svg></span>
          </div>
          <a class="icard-link" href="#fccpc-merger-thresholds" data-track="article:open:fccpc-merger-thresholds" aria-label="Read: Your Letterhead Is Now a Compliance Document — Is It Ready?"><span class="sr-only">Read: Your Letterhead Is Now a Compliance Document — Is It Ready?</span></a>
        </article>
        <article class="icard filterable reveal" id="ndpa-audit-filing-guide" data-topic="tech-ai" data-type="Guide" data-author="Senior Associate, Tech & AI">
          <div class="icard-media">
            <img src="https://resource.scp-law.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/08/WhatsApp-Image-2026-08-14-at-7.55.11-AM.jpeg" alt="" loading="lazy" decoding="async" />
            <span class="icard-type">Guide</span>
          </div>
          <div class="icard-body">
            <p class="icard-meta"><time>16 August 2026</time><span class="icard-sep" aria-hidden="true"></span><span class="icard-author">Senior Associate, Tech & AI</span></p>
            <h3 class="icard-title">Device Binding and Transaction Caps: The CBN&rsquo;s Instant Payment Guidelines Take Effect</h3>
            <p class="icard-desc">The CBN&rsquo;s Guidelines on Instant Payment Functionalities came into force on 1 July 2026, setting new minimum security standards.</p>
            <span class="icard-cta">Read<svg class="icard-arrow" viewBox="0 0 20 20" width="14" height="14" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false"><path d="M3 10h13M11 5l5 5-5 5" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.6" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"/></svg></span>
          </div>
          <a class="icard-link" href="#ndpa-audit-filing-guide" data-track="article:open:ndpa-audit-filing-guide" aria-label="Read: Device Binding and Transaction Caps: The CBN’s Instant Payment Guidelines Take Effect"><span class="sr-only">Read: Device Binding and Transaction Caps: The CBN’s Instant Payment Guidelines Take Effect</span></a>
        </article>
        <article class="icard filterable reveal" id="living-trusts-nigerian-jurisprudence" data-topic="wealth-management-smes" data-type="Article" data-author="Partner, Private Client">
          <div class="icard-media">
            <img src="https://resource.scp-law.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/08/WhatsApp-Image-2026-08-14-at-8.36.04-AM.jpeg" alt="" loading="lazy" decoding="async" />
            <span class="icard-type">Article</span>
          </div>
          <div class="icard-body">
            <p class="icard-meta"><time>16 August 2026</time><span class="icard-sep" aria-hidden="true"></span><span class="icard-author">Partner, Private Client</span></p>
            <h3 class="icard-title">Nigeria&rsquo;s 2026 Fiscal Policy Measures: What Tariff Cuts Mean for Businesses</h3>
            <p class="icard-desc">The revised tariff regime is operational, and the new excise duty regime and green tax surcharge took effect on 1 July 2026.</p>
            <span class="icard-cta">Read<svg class="icard-arrow" viewBox="0 0 20 20" width="14" height="14" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false"><path d="M3 10h13M11 5l5 5-5 5" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.6" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"/></svg></span>
          </div>
          <a class="icard-link" href="#living-trusts-nigerian-jurisprudence" data-track="article:open:living-trusts-nigerian-jurisprudence" aria-label="Read: Nigeria’s 2026 Fiscal Policy Measures: What Tariff Cuts Mean for Businesses"><span class="sr-only">Read: Nigeria’s 2026 Fiscal Policy Measures: What Tariff Cuts Mean for Businesses</span></a>
        </article>
        <article class="icard filterable reveal" id="customs-amendments-logistics" data-topic="international-trade-law" data-type="Article" data-author="Senior Associate, Trade">
          <div class="icard-media">
            <img src="https://resource.scp-law.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/08/WhatsApp-Image-2026-08-14-at-11.45.53-AM.jpeg" alt="" loading="lazy" decoding="async" />
            <span class="icard-type">Article</span>
          </div>
          <div class="icard-body">
            <p class="icard-meta"><time>16 August 2026</time><span class="icard-sep" aria-hidden="true"></span><span class="icard-author">Senior Associate, Trade</span></p>
            <h3 class="icard-title">Nigeria Harmonises Virtual Asset Regulation: The Presidential Executive Order on Virtual Assets Coordination, 2026</h3>
            <p class="icard-desc">On 17 July 2026 the President signed the Executive Order harmonising oversight of virtual assets across Nigeria&rsquo;s regulators.</p>
            <span class="icard-cta">Read<svg class="icard-arrow" viewBox="0 0 20 20" width="14" height="14" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false"><path d="M3 10h13M11 5l5 5-5 5" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.6" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"/></svg></span>
          </div>
          <a class="icard-link" href="#customs-amendments-logistics" data-track="article:open:customs-amendments-logistics" aria-label="Read: Nigeria Harmonises Virtual Asset Regulation: The Presidential Executive Order on Virtual Assets Coordination, 2026"><span class="sr-only">Read: Nigeria Harmonises Virtual Asset Regulation: The Presidential Executive Order on Virtual Assets Coordination, 2026</span></a>
        </article>
        <article class="icard filterable reveal" id="workplace-arbitration-trends" data-topic="labour-employment" data-type="Article" data-author="Partner, Labour">
          <div class="icard-media">
            <img src="https://resource.scp-law.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/08/WhatsApp-Image-2026-08-14-at-7.55.12-AM-1.jpeg" alt="" loading="lazy" decoding="async" />
            <span class="icard-type">Article</span>
          </div>
          <div class="icard-body">
            <p class="icard-meta"><time>16 August 2026</time><span class="icard-sep" aria-hidden="true"></span><span class="icard-author">Partner, Labour</span></p>
            <h3 class="icard-title">The Tax Acts 2025 Transition Guidelines: What They Mean for Estates, Trusts and Family Wealth</h3>
            <p class="icard-desc">The Ministry of Finance&rsquo;s transition guidelines clarify how the Nigeria Tax Act 2025 applies as the repealed tax laws fall away.</p>
            <span class="icard-cta">Read<svg class="icard-arrow" viewBox="0 0 20 20" width="14" height="14" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false"><path d="M3 10h13M11 5l5 5-5 5" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.6" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"/></svg></span>
          </div>
          <a class="icard-link" href="#workplace-arbitration-trends" data-track="article:open:workplace-arbitration-trends" aria-label="Read: The Tax Acts 2025 Transition Guidelines: What They Mean for Estates, Trusts and Family Wealth"><span class="sr-only">Read: The Tax Acts 2025 Transition Guidelines: What They Mean for Estates, Trusts and Family Wealth</span></a>
        </article>
        <article class="icard filterable reveal" id="digital-lending-conduct-report" data-topic="consumer-credit-dml" data-type="Report" data-author="Consumer Credit team">
          <div class="icard-media">
            <img src="https://resource.scp-law.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/08/WhatsApp-Image-2026-08-14-at-7.55.12-AM-2.jpeg" alt="" loading="lazy" decoding="async" />
            <span class="icard-type">Report</span>
          </div>
          <div class="icard-body">
            <p class="icard-meta"><time>15 August 2026</time><span class="icard-sep" aria-hidden="true"></span><span class="icard-author">Consumer Credit team</span></p>
            <h3 class="icard-title">M&amp;A Market Outlook: Fewer, Bigger and Harder to Clear</h3>
            <p class="icard-desc">Deal activity has shifted towards larger, strategically significant acquisitions in telecoms, energy, financial services and digital infrastructure.</p>
            <span class="icard-cta">Read<svg class="icard-arrow" viewBox="0 0 20 20" width="14" height="14" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false"><path d="M3 10h13M11 5l5 5-5 5" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.6" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"/></svg></span>
          </div>
          <a class="icard-link" href="#digital-lending-conduct-report" data-track="article:open:digital-lending-conduct-report" aria-label="Read: M&A Market Outlook: Fewer, Bigger and Harder to Clear"><span class="sr-only">Read: M&A Market Outlook: Fewer, Bigger and Harder to Clear</span></a>
        </article>
        <article class="icard filterable reveal" id="pia-host-community-trusts" data-topic="energy" data-type="Report" data-author="Energy team">
          <div class="icard-media">
            <img src="https://resource.scp-law.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/07/WhatsApp-Image-2026-07-19-at-8.31.29-AM.jpeg" alt="" loading="lazy" decoding="async" />
            <span class="icard-type">Report</span>
          </div>
          <div class="icard-body">
            <p class="icard-meta"><time>22 July 2026</time><span class="icard-sep" aria-hidden="true"></span><span class="icard-author">Energy team</span></p>
            <h3 class="icard-title">Allowance or Loan? What the Court&rsquo;s Approach Means for Recovery After Termination</h3>
            <p class="icard-desc">A senior hire is given a car grant, housing allowance and relocation support, to be earned back over time. Then employment ends early.</p>
            <span class="icard-cta">Read<svg class="icard-arrow" viewBox="0 0 20 20" width="14" height="14" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false"><path d="M3 10h13M11 5l5 5-5 5" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.6" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"/></svg></span>
          </div>
          <a class="icard-link" href="#pia-host-community-trusts" data-track="article:open:pia-host-community-trusts" aria-label="Read: Allowance or Loan? What the Court’s Approach Means for Recovery After Termination"><span class="sr-only">Read: Allowance or Loan? What the Court’s Approach Means for Recovery After Termination</span></a>
        </article>
        <article class="icard filterable reveal" id="transfer-pricing-defence-guide" data-topic="tax-advisory" data-type="Guide" data-author="Partner, Tax">
          <div class="icard-media">
            <img src="https://resource.scp-law.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/07/WhatsApp-Image-2026-07-19-at-8.31.39-AM1.jpeg" alt="" loading="lazy" decoding="async" />
            <span class="icard-type">Guide</span>
          </div>
          <div class="icard-body">
            <p class="icard-meta"><time>22 July 2026</time><span class="icard-sep" aria-hidden="true"></span><span class="icard-author">Partner, Tax</span></p>
            <h3 class="icard-title">Patient Data, Real Liability: What the NDPA Means for Healthcare SMEs</h3>
            <p class="icard-desc">Patient records, laboratory results, prescriptions and billing data are all now governed by the NDPA and the GAID.</p>
            <span class="icard-cta">Read<svg class="icard-arrow" viewBox="0 0 20 20" width="14" height="14" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false"><path d="M3 10h13M11 5l5 5-5 5" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.6" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"/></svg></span>
          </div>
          <a class="icard-link" href="#transfer-pricing-defence-guide" data-track="article:open:transfer-pricing-defence-guide" aria-label="Read: Patient Data, Real Liability: What the NDPA Means for Healthcare SMEs"><span class="sr-only">Read: Patient Data, Real Liability: What the NDPA Means for Healthcare SMEs</span></a>
        </article>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

